{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfiFZeJ95bUPf5UrinVYu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X3qTDDQZDhEWngMRzrfJJr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_3\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `length_normalised_chance_vs_motif`: people still judge a sequence random to the extent their model of a fair coin explains it better than the regular generators (a switch-biased Markov coin, a biased coin, and a repeating short motif with occasional slips), with the generators' unknowns averaged out and the evidence weighed per flip by a fitted power of length. The single change is that each person holds their own belief about how often a fair coin switches, drawn from a population distribution, instead of everyone sharing one over-alternating belief — so some people believe chance switches a lot while others believe chance is streaky and choose the sequence with fewer switches, addressing the critique that far more participants prefer fewer-switch sequences than the incumbent's shared belief allows.\nEOF\necho person_specific_chance_switch_belief > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'PY'\nsrc=open(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/models/length_normalised_chance_vs_motif.py\").read()\nD=\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_3\"\nhead_end=src.index('\"\"\"',3)+3\ndoc='''\"\"\"Per-person belief about a fair coin's switch rate in the Bayesian chance-vs-motif judgment.\n\nRefinement of `length_normalised_chance_vs_motif`: a sequence looks random to\nthe extent a fair coin (believed to switch with probability q) explains it\nbetter than the regular generators (Markov coin, biased coin, repeating motif\nwith slips; unknowns integrated out), the log evidence difference weighed per\nflip by (n / 5) ** -gamma, with person-specific decision sensitivity.\n\nSingle change: the believed switch probability of a fair coin is person-specific\n(non-centred logit-normal population, 400 slots), so some people believe chance\nover-alternates and others believe it is streaky (preferring fewer switches).\n\"\"\"'''\nbody=src[head_end:]\nold='''    # Believed switch probability of a fair coin (logit scale; 0 = normative).\n    logit_q = pm.Normal(\"logit_q\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n    q = pm.Deterministic(\"q\", pm.math.sigmoid(logit_q))\n'''\nnew='''    # Person-specific believed switch probability of a fair coin (logit scale;\n    # 0 = normative), non-centred population.\n    mu_logit_q = pm.Normal(\"mu_logit_q\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_logit_q = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_logit_q\", sigma=0.5)\n    z_q = pm.Normal(\"z_q\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=400)\n    logit_q = mu_logit_q + sigma_logit_q * z_q\n'''\nassert old in body\nbody=body.replace(old,new)\no2=\"score_diff = (switch_diff * logit_q - log_regular_diff) * length_scale\"\nassert o2 in body\nbody=body.replace(o2,\"score_diff = (switch_diff * logit_q[participant_id] - log_regular_diff) * length_scale\")\nopen(D+\"/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(doc+body)\nPY\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3115,"cache_read_input_tokens":60748,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3115,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","infer